Refactoring
[32] [done] Refactor the trackview.py monolith into a trackview/ package.
     Split the single-file script into focused submodules (geometry, the
     metadata/filter helpers, then parsing / rendering / stats / I/O -- see
     PLAN.md), one module at a time, each a byte-for-byte move so behaviour is
     unchanged and the test suite stays green.  A top-level trackview/ package
     would shadow the same-named trackview.py module (`import trackview` picks the
     package), so trackview/__init__.py is a re-export bridge: it loads the
     monolith as the private submodule trackview._main (importlib, from its file)
     and mirrors its namespace back into the package, so `import trackview`,
     `python trackview.py`, and `from trackview.<mod> import ...` all keep working
     under one import name (`__file__` stays the monolith's real path, so its
     `Path(__file__).parent` config -- gpx/, output/, stats/, tiles/ -- still
     resolves to the repo root).  The monolith re-imports each extracted name back
     (names used only inside a moved block stay private to that submodule); the
     bridge is deleted once every module has moved.  DONE (2026-09-30):
     geometry (Phase 1.1, trackview/geometry.py -- latlon_to_merc, decimate,
     _distance_and_gain, _grade_and_cumkm, PI_R), the metadata/filter/selection
     helpers (Phase 1.2, trackview/helpers.py -- the Wahoo-stem date + device/sport
     <desc> readers, the --since/--until / --device/--sport / --top filters and the
     string helpers) and the metric/telemetry/calorie/formatting helpers (Phase 1.3,
     trackview/metrics.py -- _point_telemetry, the per-track/ride metric averages and
     steepest grades, the robust grade-colour cap, the power x time calorie estimate and
     the shared "value or a dash" formatters; the 6 boundary constants stay private, the
     11 functions are re-imported, and the 4 TestGradeCap cases now read GRADE_CAP_* from
     trackview.metrics).  Remaining: the rendering cluster (_metric_norm, _moving_avg,
     the colour constants and the render/write_* figures -- Phase 1.4), then stats and
     I/O (1.5-1.6).

     DONE (2026-09-30, Phase 1.4a): the *leaf* rendering helpers --
     trackview/rendering.py holds _metric_norm (the robust percentile colour
     norm), _moving_avg (the centred, NaN-skipping moving average) and the three
     constants CMAPEED (the "inferno" effort ramp), GRADE_CBAR_MAX (4.0, the max
     per-ride grade colourbars on a combined map) and SUPPRESSED_RENDER_DEVICES
     ({"Kickr Snap"}, a trainer's route-less session kept off the image but still
     logged).  Copied byte-for-byte so behaviour is unchanged; rendering.py is
     leaner than metrics.py -- it imports only numpy + matplotlib.colors.Normalize,
     with no back-edge to the monolith and no metrics dependency.  All 5 names are
     still used by code that stays in the monolith (render colours by CMAPEED via
     _metric_norm; the profile and _ride_climbs run _moving_avg over a GRADE_SMOOTH
     window; main keeps SUPPRESSED tags off the image), so all 5 are re-imported and
     none is private to the module.  No test changes: tv._moving_avg resolves via the
     bridge and the 3 constants + _metric_norm have no test references.  101 pass, 1
     skip.  Remaining under Phase 1.4: the render/write_* figure cluster (1.4b,
     matplotlib-coupled, a back-edge to _load_basemap/decimate/_short_label/
     _title_name/_load_stats -- waits until those helpers move), then stats (1.5)
     and I/O (1.6).

     DONE (2026-09-30, Phase 1.4b-i): the profile / heat / scale-bar *drawing*
