Build & packaging
[33] [done] Add a build system (PLAN Phase 6.1): package metadata, dependency
     management and a console entry point.  The plan named `setup.py`, but the repo
     already held a `requirements.txt` and no build file, so a legacy `setup.py` would
     sit as a third, out-of-sync source of truth -- the config is therefore PEP 518/621
     in `pyproject.toml` (`[build-system]` + `[project]`, backend `setuptools.build_meta`):
     metadata (name `trackview`, version `0.1.0`, a one-line description, `readme =
     "README.md"`, `requires-python = ">=3.10"`), the runtime `dependencies` (contextily /
     gpxpy / matplotlib / numpy -- the versions mirrored from `requirements.txt`, which
     stays as the `pip install -r` convenience), two optional extras (`fit = fitparse`,
     used only by the top-level `fit_to_gpx.py`, not the package; `test = pytest`), and
     the console entry point `[project.scripts] trackview = "trackview.cli:main"` -- the
     installed counterpart to `python trackview.py` (the root launcher re-enters this
     same `main`).  A `[tool.setuptools] packages = ["trackview"]` stops flat-layout
     auto-discovery sweeping the root `trackview.py` launcher or the data/script dirs
     (gpx/ output/ stats/ tiles/ fit/ gc/ lib/ tools/) into the build; the same file also
     carries the pre-existing `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` (`testpaths`, the `network` /
     `slow` markers), so it is the single source of truth for build *and* test-runner
     config.
     DONE (2026-10-18): a real PEP 517 build (`python -m build`, in a throwaway venv so
     the main `.venv` stayed untouched) produced a clean sdist + `trackview-0.1.0-
     py3-none-any.whl`: `top_level.txt` / `RECORD` list only the `trackview/` submodules
     (the root `trackview.py` and every data dir excluded), `entry_points.txt` =
     `trackview = trackview.cli:main`, and `METADATA` carries the four core deps + the two
     extras.  No behaviour changed; offline suite: 211 passed, 1 deselected.


