     carry one, in the house style (role + behaviour prose) -- trackview/cli.main (the
     CLI orchestrator: parse the flags, run the filter sequence, dispatch to the writers)
     and trackview/mapfig.render (the map / ride-card / heat figure pipeline); a quick
     AST scan now reports every module and every function carries a docstring.  The
     0-byte trackview/__init__.py gained a short package docstring (the tool's one-line
     purpose, that it is a regular re-export-free package whose submodules are imported by
     full name, a pointer to API.md); it still re-exports nothing, so the package stays a
     namespace for the extracted leaves, not a second monolith.  A new top-level API.md
     catalogs the module map: for each of the 13 modules its role, the constants it holds
     and its functions (signature + first docstring line), the programmatic entry points
     (load_tracks -> the write_* reports / render / write_gallery), the acyclic dependency
     direction, and an honest note that the leading-underscore helpers are the
     carried-over monolith names that *are* the cross-module API (there is no __all__, so
     the module boundaries -- not the _ -- are the interface).  Usage examples stay in
     README.md (its full Usage section), which API.md points to rather than duplicating.
     API.md is a top-level doc, not shipped (the build declares packages = ["trackview"],
     so it ships only the trackview/ package).  No behaviour changed; offline suite:
     211 passed, 1 deselected.
